# Environment template — safe placeholders only.
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` files are git-ignored and must
# never be committed. No real values, IDs, URLs, keys or tokens belong in this file.
#
# PUBLIC_ENV and PUBLIC_ALLOW_DEMO_FACTS are read by the content policy
# (src/lib/content/policy.ts). The remaining names are reserved so that later
# phases have a single, documented place to add configuration.

# Canonical site origin, used for absolute URLs, canonical tags and the sitemap.
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:4321"

# Build environment: development | staging | production
# PUBLIC_ENV="development"

# Affiliate destination. Stays disabled until a real, approved URL is supplied.
# PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_ENABLED="false"
# PUBLIC_AFFILIATE_URL=""

# Analytics. Provider-agnostic; no provider is installed yet.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=""
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=""

# Content safety gate. When "false", any fact still marked demo/needs-review
# fails the build rather than being rendered.
#
# May only TIGHTEN the policy: production blocks demo facts unconditionally and
# no value here can re-enable them. Must be exactly "true" or "false" if set —
# any other value fails the build. See docs/CONTENT.md.
# PUBLIC_ALLOW_DEMO_FACTS="true"
